on), including Babylonia and the Babylonian empire}"],"H3679":["כַּסְדַּי","Kaçday","kas-dah'-ee","{a Kasdite, or descendant of Kesed; by implication, a Chaldaean (as if so descended); also an astrologer (as if proverbial of that people}"],"H5642":["סְתַר","çᵉthar","seth-ar'","to conceal; figuratively, to demolish"],"H5972":["עַם","ʻam","am","{a people (as a congregated unit); specifically, a tribe (as those of Israel); hence (collectively) troops or attendants; figuratively, a flock}"],"H1541":["גְּלָה","gᵉlâh","ghel-aw'","{to denude (especially in a disgraceful sense); by implication, to exile (captives being usually stripped); figuratively, to reveal}"],"H1297":["בְּרַם","bᵉram","ber-am'","properly, highly, i.e. surely; but used adversatively, however"],"H2298":["חַד","chad","khad","as card. one; as article single; as an ordinal, first; adverbially, at once"],"H3567":["כּוֹרֶשׁ","Kôwresh","ko'-resh","{Koresh (or Cyrus), the Persian king}"],"H3984":["מָאן","mâʼn","mawn","a utensil"],"H1722":["דְּהַב","dᵉhab","deh-hab'","gold"],"H3702":["כְּסַף","kᵉçaph","kes-af'","{silver (from its pale color); by implication, money}"],"H5312":["נְפַק","nᵉphaq","nef-ak'","to issue; causatively, to bring out"],"H1965":["הֵיכַל","hêykal","hay-kal'","{a large public building, such as a palace or temple}"],"H2987":["יְבַל","yᵉbal","yeb-al'","to bring"],"H8340":["שֵׁשְׁבַּצַּר","Shêshᵉbatstsar","shaysh-bats-tsar'","{Sheshbatstsar, Zerubbabel's Persian name}"],"H412":["אֵל","ʼêl","ale","{these or those}"],"H5376":["נְשָׂא","nᵉsâʼ","nes-aw'","{to lift}"],"H5182":["נְחַת","nᵉchath","nekh-ath'","to descend; causatively, to bring away, deposit, depose"],"H870":["אֲתַר","ʼăthar","ath-ar'","a place; (adverb) after"],"H787":["אֹשׁ","ʼôsh","ohsh","a foundation"],"H3705":["כְּעַן","kᵉʻan","keh-an'","now"],"H8000":["שְׁלַם","shᵉlam","shel-am'","to complete, to restore"],"H2006":["הֵן","hên","hane","lo! also there(-fore), (un-) less, whether, but, if"],"H2869":["טָב","ṭâb","teh-abe'","good"],"H124